lesson: 165
title: Working together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When two teams work at the same time, their work for one day adds up: what both do together in a day is the sum.
explain: One team lays 30 m of road a day, the other 20 m: together they lay 30 + 20 = 50 m a day.
explain: A road of 250 m then takes them 250 / 50 = 5 days.
vars: a=name b=name p=10..60 q=10..60 d=2..9 g=2..4
need: (p + q) * d <= 900
answer: d
exercise: One team lays {p} metres of road a day and another team lays {q} metres a day. Working together, how many days do they need for {(p+q)*d} metres of road?
exercise: {a} can pick {p} apples an hour and {b} can pick {q} apples an hour. How many hours will it take them together to pick {(p+q)*d} apples?
exercise: One machine prints {p} pages a minute and another prints {q} pages a minute. Both print at once. How many minutes do they need for {(p+q)*d} pages?
exercise: A tank is filled through two pipes. One pipe lets in {p} litres a minute and the other {q} litres a minute. How many minutes does it take to fill {(p+q)*d} litres with both pipes open?
exercise: Workshop A sews {p} shirts a day and workshop B sews {q} shirts a day. An order is for {(p+q)*d} shirts. In how many days do the two workshops finish it together?
exercise: A team can dig {p*g} metres of ditch in {g} days, and a second team digs {q} metres a day. How many days do both teams together need to dig {(p+q)*d} metres?
test: How long, in days, does it take two crews to paint a fence {(p+q)*d} metres long if one paints {p} metres a day and the other {q} metres a day, side by side?
test: {a} types {p} words a minute and {b} types {q} words a minute. They share the typing of a {(p+q)*d}-word story. How many minutes does the story take them?
test: Two bakeries get an order for {(p+q)*d} loaves. The first bakes {p*g} loaves in {g} days, the second {q} loaves a day. Baking at the same time, how many days do they need?
test: Pump A drains {p} buckets of water an hour and pump B drains {q}. Working at once, the pumps empty a pond of {(p+q)*d} buckets. How many hours did that take?
exercise: Two crews in Ohio build a fence {(p+q)*d} metres long together. One crew builds {p} metres a day and the other {q} metres a day. How many days does the fence take?
exercise: How many hours do {a} and {b} need to pick {(p+q)*d} strawberries together if {a} picks {p} an hour and {b} picks {q} an hour?
exercise: Two printers in a library in London print at the same time. The first does {p} pages per minute, the second {q} pages per minute. How long, in minutes, do {(p+q)*d} pages take?
exercise: A pool in Queensland is filled by two hoses at once. One gives {p} litres a minute, the other {q} litres a minute. How many minutes pass until {(p+q)*d} litres are in the pool?
exercise: {a} bakes {p} cookies an hour and {b} bakes {q} cookies an hour. Working side by side, how many hours do they take to bake {(p+q)*d} cookies for a fair in Vermont?
exercise: Two machines bottle juice at once, {p} bottles a minute and {q} bottles a minute. How many minutes does it take them to fill {(p+q)*d} bottles combined?
exercise: One team paints {p*g} metres of wall in {g.words} days; another paints {q} metres per day. How many days do the two teams need together for {(p+q)*d} metres?
exercise: {(p+q)*d} boxes must be packed. {a} packs {p} boxes an hour and {b} packs {q} boxes an hour. If both pack at the same time, how many hours does it take?
test: {a} knits {p} rows a day and {b} knits {q} rows a day. Together they knit a scarf of {(p+q)*d} rows for a charity in Dublin. How many days does it take?
test: Find how many minutes two taps running at the same time take to fill a tub with {(p+q)*d} litres, if one tap runs {p} litres a minute and the other {q}.
test: A digger in Alberta moves {p*g} tonnes of earth in {g} hours, and a second digger moves {q} tonnes an hour. Working at once, in how many hours do they move {(p+q)*d} tonnes?
test: Two farmers in Wales plough a field at once; one ploughs {p} rows a day, the other {q}. The field has {(p+q)*d} rows. How long, in days, does it take?
test: Two teams of volunteers clean a beach in New Zealand. One collects {p} bags of rubbish a day, the other {q}. How many days pass until they have collected {(p+q)*d} bags between them?
test: With two scanners working together, one scanning {q} photos a minute and the other {p}, how many minutes does it take to scan {(p+q)*d} photos?
exercise: one team does {p} m of road a day other does {q}, how many days together for {(p+q)*d} m
exercise: {a} picks {p} apples an hour, {b} {q+2} — no wait, {q} an hour. how many hours for {(p+q)*d} apples together
exercise: two pipes, {p} and {q} litres a min, tank's {(p+q)*d} litres, oh and the tank's blue lol. how many mins to fill
exercise: Sam says just do the big number ÷ {p}. nah wrong innit, both are workin. printers do {p} and {q} pages a min, {(p+q)*d} pages, how many mins
test: two crews paintin a fence {(p+q)*d} m, one does {p} a day other {q}, how many days it take em
test: {a} types {p} words a min, {b} does {q}, story's {(p+q)*d} words, {a} made {g} typos lol. how many mins
test: Sam reckons {d+1} hours?? wrong innit. pumps do {p} and {q} buckets an hour, pond's {(p+q)*d} buckets, how many hours really
exercise: Since the factory let half its workers go, only two crews are left: one packs {p} boxes a day and the other packs {q} boxes a day. Together, how many days do they need for {(p+q)*d} boxes?
exercise: grandad's popped his clogs and his garden's a bloody jungle. {a} pulls {p} weeds an hour, {b} pulls {q}. {(p+q)*d} weeds. how many hours, and quit moaning
test: {a} and {b} are "between jobs", so they take a cleaning job together: {(p+q)*d} plates to wash, {a} washing {p} plates an hour and {b} {q} plates an hour. How long does the job take, in hours?
exam: It is given that one team lays {p} metres of road per day and a second team {q} metres per day. Determine the number of days required for both teams, working jointly, to lay {(p+q)*d} metres of road.
exam: Whereas {a} picks {p} apples per hour and {b} picks {q} apples per hour, ascertain the number of hours required for the two of them, working together, to pick {(p+q)*d} apples.
exam: Two pumps, delivering {p} litres and {q} litres per minute respectively, are set in operation simultaneously to fill an empty tank of {(p+q)*d} litres. Ascertain the number of minutes requisite for the filling of the tank.
exam: A document of {(p+q)*d} pages is to be typed by two clerks working concurrently, the first typing {p} pages per day and the second {q} pages per day. State the number of days required for the completion of the document.
